Ubuntu Touch for Samsung Tab S9 Ultra Wi-Fi SM-X910 (gts9uwifi) - flashable package

The installer ZIP (built by scripts/make-flashable.sh after build.sh +
scripts/super.sh) flashes from TWRP exactly these partitions:

  boot, init_boot, vendor_boot, vbmeta, super

It refuses to run on any device not positively identified as SM-X910
(ro.product.device gts9u/gts9uwifi AND ro.boot.em.model SM-X910, with a
bootloader X910* fallback check).

It never writes: recovery, dtbo, userdata, metadata, efs, sec_efs, persist,
modemst1/2, or any bootloader-stage partition (xbl*, abl, aop, tz, hyp,
devcfg, keymaster, uefisecapp, qupfw, storsec). It never repartitions,
never wipes, and never reboots by itself.

The super image is assembled locally with lpmake from the Ubuntu Touch rootfs
(system) plus the stock SM-X910 dynamic partition images (vendor, odm,
product, system_ext, system_dlkm, vendor_dlkm extracted from official
X910XXS5CYG1 firmware; vendor_dlkm has the rebuilt kernel modules swapped
in). Samsung images are proprietary: they are never committed to git and
never redistributed inside this repository.

Restore path: every partition the installer writes is restored by flashing
the official SM-X910 firmware (AP + BL + CSC) with Odin. See
docs/recovery-sm-x910.md in the port workspace.
